cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VRAMZ in research or technical work, please cite this software."
title: "VRAMZ: Experimental GPU-Resident Compressed-Memory Runtime"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nezer
    given-names: Rami
version: "1.0.0-rc1-research"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  VRAMZ is an experimental userspace runtime for NVIDIA GPUs that explores
  lossless GPU-resident compression, CUDA VMM-backed storage, adaptive reclaim,
  and exact physical-backing accounting to increase effective logical GPU
  capacity for explicitly integrated applications.
keywords:
  - gpu
  - cuda
  - memory
  - compression
  - vmm
  - nvcomp
  - research
